<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodore I Palaiologos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1355–<a href="/years/1407">1407</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodore I Palaiologos was the Byzantine Despot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a> from 1383 to 1407, a son of Emperor John V. He strengthened Byzantine rule in the Peloponnese, settled Albanian colonists there and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, the Navarrese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. In 1388 he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a>, which Venice had just bought from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marie-of-enghien">Marie of Enghien</a>, but he was forced to hand it over to Venice in 1394.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodore-i-palaiologos.jpg" alt="Theodore I Palaiologos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ΣΕΒΑΣΤΟΚΡΑΤΩΡ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%CE%A4%CE%BF%CE%B9%CF%87%CE%BF%CE%B3%CF%81%CE%B1%CF%86%CE%AF%CE%B1_%CE%B1%CF%80%CE%BF_%CF%84%CE%BF%CE%BD_%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%86%CE%BF_%CF%84%CE%BF%CF%85_%CE%B4%CE%B5%CF%83%CF%80%CF%8C%CF%84%CE%B7_%CE%98%CE%B5%CF%8C%CE%B4%CF%89%CF%81%CE%BF%CF%85_%CE%91%CE%84_%CE%A0%CE%B1%CE%BB%CE%B1%CE%B9%CE%BF%CE%BB%CF%8C%CE%B3%CE%BF%CF%85_%CF%80%CE%BF%CF%85_%CF%84%CE%BF%CE%BD_%CE%B1%CE%BD%CE%B1%CF%80%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CF%83%CF%84%CE%AC_%CF%89%CF%82_%CE%B7%CE%B3%CE%B5%CE%BC%CF%8C%CE%BD%CE%B1_%CE%BA%CE%B1%CE%B9_%CE%BC%CE%BF%CE%BD%CE%B1%CF%87%CF%8C.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
